# Proof of Concept (PoC) Technical Report
**Project Name:** FinPay Cloud Security Architecture & Threat Vector Validation  
**Author:** Security Engineering & Architecture Team  
**Date:** September 2026  
**Document Classification:** Internal / Confidential  

---

## 1. Executive Summary
This Proof of Concept (PoC) evaluates the security posture and architectural trust boundaries of **FinPay Core Services**, a multi-tier cloud-native payment application. The objective was to validate high-risk threats identified during STRIDE/DREAD threat modeling and determine whether architectural controls effectively prevent identity spoofing, broken object-level authorization (BOLA), and internal data exfiltration.

The PoC confirmed two critical design vulnerabilities:
1. **Broken Object Level Authorization (BOLA)** on the payment capture endpoint (`/v1/payment/capture`), enabling unauthorized account balance debits.
2. **Insecure Interservice Communication**, allowing cleartext token inspection and potential request forgery across the internal Kubernetes service mesh.

